<title>USA: Clark Ill. plant hearing restarts Thursday.</title>
<headline>Clark Ill. plant hearing restarts Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A hearing over whether or not to shut Clark Refining and Marketing Co's 80,515 barrels-per-day (bpd) oil refinery at Blue Island, Illinois will carry through to Thursday, a spokesman for the Illinois Attorney General said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The hearing started Wednesday at the Cook County Circuit Court after the Attorney General, Dan Curry, sought a court order to shut the plant after a fire there last Saturday.</p>
<p>The plant is located near a residential area, including a nearby high school, and Curry wants the entire plant shut pending a safety investigation.</p>
